      "playbook": [
        "Treat any password used during the Telnet sessions to `10.10.0.20:23` as exposed. Plan a rotation with the on-shift engineer for those devices and any account whose credentials may be reused (a Telnet password on a switch is often the same engineer account used elsewhere).",
        "Migrate the listed devices to SSH where they support it. The asset inventory shows which hosts also speak the secure equivalent — use that as the starting list.",
        "For devices without a secure alternative (older Moxa serial servers, legacy HMIs, managed switches that only support Telnet), place behind a jump host on a hardened management VLAN. Document the exception with a revocation date.",
        "Record the credentials-exposed window in the change log so future investigations know which sessions to consider compromised. Capture window: see report header."
